Composery product identity and defaults - everything that makes the assembled
IDE present as Composery rather than code-server, plus the out-of-box defaults
we ship.

- product.json coordinates: Composery documentation/newsletter URLs, trusted
  domains, server data folder; letterpress and window-icon SVGs replaced with
  the brand mark.
- Welcome: the Coder promo block becomes the "Set up an AI coding agent" card
  grid (composery.installAgent via the composery-agents builtin); the
  COMPOSERY_DISABLE_GETTING_STARTED_OVERRIDE gate is kept. Welcome slides
  scroll natively on touch (never Gesture-target them - a registered target
  preventDefault()s touchend and kills every plain click in the page).
- Watermark: workspace tips reduced to commands/goto/recent.
- Extensions view: the default "Popular" list becomes "Themes"
  (category:themes @popular) - themes are the one kind of extension every
  fresh instance wants.
- Default layout: views hidden by default until a user opts in (outline,
  timeline, npm, scm repositories, recommended extensions), only where no
  stored visibility exists; view containers left off their bar the same way
  (run and debug, output, debug console) plus the accounts entry. Both are
  first-run defaults expressed in upstream's own state - a hidden view is
  hideByDefault, an absent container is simply unpinned - so the bar's context
  menu puts either back and the choice persists. Nothing is re-evaluated
  against the id lists once the user has seen the container. Container
  LOCATIONS are deliberately not touched: moving scm/markers/extensions/
  terminal between bars is a layout opinion, not a default, and it lived in
  per-browser storage where it could not survive a second device anyway.
- Menubar: web-navigation actions belong to the File root, not every nested
  submenu (upstream appended them to both).
- Titlebar: the Composery home button/logo, with its context menu.
- Composery Dark / Composery Light as default color themes, including
  upstream's synchronous first-paint snapshot retinted with the
  composery-themes values - the "default color theme" tests fail if the
  snapshot drifts from the theme JSONs.
- Terminal: shortcuts.contribution.ts bridges internal services for the
  composery-shortcuts builtin; 4px top/bottom terminal padding
  (TerminalInstance._getDimension subtracts computed padding, so this
  reserves real rows instead of clipping).

